{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Emergence.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Emergence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"emergence emergence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Emergence.md","fileName":"Emergence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Emergence","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Emergent Systems]] [[Emergent Game Narrative]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Emergent Systems","Emergent Game Narrative","Modular Behavior","Downward Causality","Upward Causality","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Emergence.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Emergence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"emergence emergence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Emergence.md","fileName":"Emergence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Emergence","heading":"Emergence","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Emergence is the appearance of a relatively stable property or behavior at the level of a whole that is qualitatively different from the properties of its individual parts. It is produced by distributed interactions rather than directed by one component.\n\nLocal, generic [[Modular Behavior|behaviors]] and feedback loops make emergence possible. The resulting whole can in turn affect its parts through [[Downward Causality]], while the parts create it through [[Upward Causality]].\n\nIn games, emergence can appear as a strategy, event, or story that no author explicitly sequenced. It arises from the player's choices interacting with the system and may differ substantially between sessions using the same rules.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Emergent Systems","Emergent Game Narrative","Modular Behavior","Downward Causality","Upward Causality","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvoca